properties.statement:
When a step loses a premise, its conclusion reads UNSUPPORTED (unknown), not "fails". "fails" is kept for a claim an established objection refutes.

A what-if says, for each claim, which of three is true:
- it keeps another line of support;
- it is left unsupported;
- it is refuted.

From the primes trial, items 2 and 9 (friction F13, F24). @ajs, 2026-10-17.
